{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "fixtureId": "tls-gateway-frame-v1",
  "description": [
    "Shared TLS-215 fixture: the exact bytes of the C05 LAT1 metadata frame.",
    "Kotlin reads the 'accept' entries, drives its production TlsGatewayChannel",
    "against a recording loopback gateway and asserts that the frame it writes",
    "carries exactly these seven fields with these values and this framing.",
    "Go feeds every entry - accepted and refused alike - to the real gateway",
    "reader, and asserts that the accepted metadata is what the sender meant",
    "and that each refusal happens for the recorded reason. Neither side",
    "re-implements the other: Kotlin never validates a frame it may not send,",
    "and Go never rewrites one."
  ],
  "frames": [
    {
      "id": "ipv4-candidate",
      "accept": true,
      "reason": "the ordinary case: an IPv4 destination on the candidate port",
      "captureId": "capture-1",
      "connectionId": "c1",
      "networkGeneration": 0,
      "destinationAddress": "198.51.100.7",
      "destinationPort": 443,
      "token": "AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA",
      "body": "{\"version\":1,\"captureId\":\"capture-1\",\"connectionId\":\"c1\",\"networkGeneration\":0,\"destinationAddress\":\"198.51.100.7\",\"destinationPort\":443,\"token\":\"AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA\"}"
    },
    {
